WEBVTT

00:00:00.494 --> 00:00:17.276
Simon and the Spy by Elizabeth Laird.

00:00:17.335 --> 00:00:34.328
Simon Simple is at the station.

00:00:34.388 --> 00:00:38.079
He's going on a train.

00:00:38.139 --> 00:00:41.950
There are policemen at the station.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.882
There are policemen on the trains.

00:00:45.942 --> 00:00:50.144
They're all working very hard.

00:00:50.204 --> 00:00:53.326
Why are the police here?

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.677
Simon asks a man.

00:00:55.736 --> 00:00:57.128
Look!

00:00:57.188 --> 00:00:59.362
The man says.

00:00:59.421 --> 00:01:03.476
Simon looks at the man's newspaper.

00:01:03.536 --> 00:01:06.328
Do you know this man?

00:01:06.388 --> 00:01:07.798
He reads.

00:01:07.858 --> 00:01:10.379
He's a spy.

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:11.890
Find him.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.300
Stop him.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.962
Catch him.

00:01:16.022 --> 00:01:21.054
Simon looks at the people in the station.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:27.786
He can see students in jeans and men in suits.

00:01:27.846 --> 00:01:31.786
He can see families and children.
 
00:01:31.846 --> 00:01:35.568
He can't see any spies.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:42.890
Simon's train goes at 11 and it's 1057 now.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:46.092
Simon runs to the train.

00:01:46.152 --> 00:01:50.904
There's an old woman with an umbrella near Simon.

00:01:50.964 --> 00:01:54.266
She's walking very fast.

00:01:54.325 --> 00:01:56.867
Simon doesn't see her.

00:01:56.927 --> 00:01:59.958
He doesn't see her bag.

00:02:00.018 --> 00:02:04.580
The old woman's bag hits Simon's foot.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.082
Simon falls.

00:02:07.142 --> 00:02:09.684
His bag opens.

00:02:09.744 --> 00:02:13.266
His things fall to the ground.

00:02:13.326 --> 00:02:17.250
The old woman's bag opens too.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.302
A letter falls out.

00:02:20.362 --> 00:02:24.355
Simon puts his things into his bag.

00:02:24.415 --> 00:02:28.790
The old woman's letter is with Simon's things.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:31.704
Simon doesn't see it.

00:02:31.764 --> 00:02:36.008
He puts the old woman's letter in his bag.

00:02:36.068 --> 00:02:44.544
He closes his bag and runs to the train.

00:02:44.604 --> 00:02:51.790
Simon sits down in the train.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.833
There's a beautiful girl beside him.

00:02:55.893 --> 00:02:59.204
Hello, Simon says.

00:02:59.264 --> 00:03:02.814
Hello, the girl says.

00:03:02.874 --> 00:03:06.716
The old woman's on the train too.

00:03:06.776 --> 00:03:10.739
She's looking at Simon's bag.

00:03:10.798 --> 00:03:14.240
She wants her letter.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.672
There are policemen on the train.

00:03:17.731 --> 00:03:20.994
They can't find the spy.

00:03:21.054 --> 00:03:24.605
The old woman sees the policeman.

00:03:24.665 --> 00:03:29.961
She turns and walks quickly down the train.

00:03:30.021 --> 00:03:33.306
Simon likes the girl.

00:03:33.366 --> 00:03:36.188
She likes him.

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:39.579
There's a restaurant on the train.

00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:41.450
Simon says.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:44.771
Do you want a cup of coffee?

00:03:44.831 --> 00:03:46.702
Yes, please.

00:03:46.762 --> 00:03:48.342
The girl says.

00:03:48.402 --> 00:03:49.643
Okay.

00:03:49.703 --> 00:03:53.665
Wait here. Simon says.
 
00:03:53.725 --> 00:03:58.740
Simon takes his bag and goes to the restaurant.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:02.284
The old woman's waiting for him.

00:04:02.344 --> 00:04:05.106
Simon doesn't see her.

00:04:05.166 --> 00:04:11.779
He doesn't see her foot.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:18.404
The train's going fast.

00:04:18.464 --> 00:04:20.635
Simon falls.

00:04:20.695 --> 00:04:23.816
The old woman falls too.

00:04:23.876 --> 00:04:27.379
She sits down on the floor.

00:04:27.439 --> 00:04:31.702
Oh! I'm sorry, Simon says.
 
00:04:31.762 --> 00:04:34.422
He helps the old woman.

00:04:34.482 --> 00:04:39.134
Simon sees the old woman's shoes.

00:04:39.194 --> 00:04:44.906
He looks at her shoes and he looks at her face.

00:04:44.966 --> 00:04:50.487
They're not women's shoes, Simon thinks.

00:04:50.547 --> 00:04:58.441
Simon buys the coffee and goes back to the girl.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:04.174
The train stops.

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:09.328
Simon and the girl are going on a boat now.

00:05:09.388 --> 00:05:13.451
They walk from the train to the boat.

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:17.103
There are policemen here too.

00:05:17.163 --> 00:05:21.506
What do they want? The girl asks.
 
00:05:21.566 --> 00:05:25.588
There's a spy. Simon says.
 
00:05:25.648 --> 00:05:29.562
A spy? The girl says.
 
00:05:29.621 --> 00:05:32.590
I can't see any spies.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.298
Simon looks too.

00:05:35.357 --> 00:05:39.080
He sees families and students.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:41.562
He sees the old woman.

00:05:41.622 --> 00:05:44.794
No, Simon says.

00:05:44.854 --> 00:05:51.338
I can't see any spies.

00:05:51.398 --> 00:05:57.742
It's a beautiful day.

00:05:57.802 --> 00:06:02.292
The sun's shining and the water's blue.

00:06:02.352 --> 00:06:07.922
Simon and the girl sit near the water and wait.

00:06:07.982 --> 00:06:10.594
The boat's coming.

00:06:10.654 --> 00:06:14.946
What's your name? Simon asks.
 
00:06:15.006 --> 00:06:18.728
Samantha. The girl says.
 
00:06:18.788 --> 00:06:22.090
Oh. Simon says.
 
00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:27.472
My name's Simon. Simon and Samantha.
 
00:06:27.532 --> 00:06:29.684
That's nice.

00:06:29.744 --> 00:06:33.468
Simon and Samantha are talking.

00:06:33.528 --> 00:06:36.744
They don't see the old woman.

00:06:36.804 --> 00:06:40.849
They don't see her umbrella.

00:06:40.909 --> 00:06:45.294
Look out! A man shouts.
 
00:06:45.354 --> 00:06:47.806
There's a lorry!

00:06:47.866 --> 00:06:51.340
Simon and Samantha look.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:55.584
A lorry is coming down the road very fast.

00:06:55.644 --> 00:07:01.700
They jump back.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.284
The old woman jumps back too.

00:07:05.344 --> 00:07:09.405
Simon sees her trousers.

00:07:09.465 --> 00:07:14.888
They're not women's trousers. Simon thinks.
 
00:07:14.948 --> 00:07:16.968
Come on, Simon.

00:07:17.028 --> 00:07:20.750
The boat's here. Samantha says.
 
00:07:20.809 --> 00:07:29.302
Simon and Samantha get on the boat.

00:07:29.362 --> 00:07:39.034
Simon opens his bag and takes his lunch out.

00:07:39.094 --> 00:07:45.436
He takes the old woman's letter out too, but he doesn't see it.

00:07:45.496 --> 00:07:50.779
Do you want a sandwich? Simon asks Samantha.
 
00:07:50.839 --> 00:07:54.711
Yes, please. Samantha says.
 
00:07:54.771 --> 00:07:58.472
She takes her lunch out of her bag.

00:07:58.532 --> 00:08:02.050
Do you want an apple? She says.
 
00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:05.308
The old woman's behind them.

00:08:05.368 --> 00:08:09.210
Simon and Samantha don't see her.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:12.611
They don't see her hand.

00:08:12.671 --> 00:08:16.302
The boat's going fast now.

00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:19.444
The wind's strong.

00:08:19.504 --> 00:08:23.315
Samantha's hair goes in her eyes.

00:08:23.375 --> 00:08:27.107
The wind takes the old woman's letter.

00:08:27.166 --> 00:08:30.947
The letter flies along the boat.

00:08:31.007 --> 00:08:35.308
What's that paper? Samantha says.
 
00:08:35.368 --> 00:08:37.970
Is it your boat ticket?

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:41.712
I don't know. Simon says.
 
00:08:41.772 --> 00:08:43.623
Simon runs.

00:08:43.683 --> 00:08:45.684
He wants his ticket.

00:08:45.744 --> 00:08:48.396
The old woman runs too.

00:08:48.456 --> 00:08:54.504
She wants her letter.

00:08:54.564 --> 00:09:02.144
Simon and the old woman run fast.

00:09:02.204 --> 00:09:04.400
They're near the paper now.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:09.428
What's that?

00:09:09.488 --> 00:09:11.280
It's a dog.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:13.982
He's running very fast.

00:09:14.042 --> 00:09:19.036
He runs to the paper and catches it in his mouth.

00:09:19.096 --> 00:09:22.858
My ticket! Simon says.
 
00:09:22.918 --> 00:09:27.578
My letter! The old woman says.
 
00:09:27.638 --> 00:09:30.846
The dog runs along the boat.

00:09:30.906 --> 00:09:34.589
Catch the dog. Simon says.
 
00:09:34.649 --> 00:09:38.832
Stop him. Says the old woman.
 
00:09:38.892 --> 00:09:41.284
The dog's happy.

00:09:41.344 --> 00:09:43.505
He can run fast.

00:09:43.565 --> 00:09:47.658
He's playing a game with Simon and the old woman.

00:09:47.718 --> 00:09:50.589
He doesn't see Samantha.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:54.282
Samantha jumps up and catches him.

00:09:54.342 --> 00:09:58.548
I've got him Simon. Samantha says.
 
00:09:58.608 --> 00:10:02.944
Simon and the old woman run to Samantha.

00:10:03.004 --> 00:10:06.076
The paper's in the dog's mouth.

00:10:06.136 --> 00:10:08.438
Simon looks at it.

00:10:08.498 --> 00:10:13.451
That's not my ticket. He says, no.
 
00:10:13.511 --> 00:10:19.225
The old woman says, it's my letter.

00:10:19.285 --> 00:10:27.200
The dog likes Simon and Samantha, but he doesn't like the old woman 

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:31.896
He takes her coat in his mouth and pulls it.

00:10:31.956 --> 00:10:34.738
The coat falls to the ground.

00:10:34.798 --> 00:10:38.171
The wind takes the old woman's hat.

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:40.672
It falls into the water.

00:10:40.732 --> 00:10:43.786
Her hair falls with the hat.

00:10:43.846 --> 00:10:47.868
Simon and Samantha look at the old woman.

00:10:47.928 --> 00:10:50.310
It's not an old woman.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:52.432
It's a man.

00:10:52.492 --> 00:10:56.778
The spy! Simon says.
 
00:10:56.838 --> 00:11:02.183
Police, come here!

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:08.036
The police are very happy.

00:11:08.096 --> 00:11:12.238
Thank you, Simon. They say.
 
00:11:12.298 --> 00:11:15.620
Now we have the spy.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:18.902
But the spy has a letter.

00:11:18.962 --> 00:11:23.207
The letter has names and addresses on it.

00:11:23.267 --> 00:11:27.882
We want the letter, but we can't find it.

00:11:27.942 --> 00:11:29.682
Where is it?

00:11:29.742 --> 00:11:31.784
Do you know?

00:11:31.844 --> 00:11:34.776
Simon looks at the dog.

00:11:34.836 --> 00:11:37.907
The dog looks at Simon.

00:11:37.967 --> 00:11:42.100
There's the letter. Simon says.
 
00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:45.200
Where? Says the policeman.
 
00:11:45.300 --> 00:12:08.000
It's in the dog. Simon says.
